WEBVTT

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:22.270
Welcome.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.220
That'll be 420 yen.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:30.210
Thank you very much.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:42.190
She probably seemed familiar 
because her hair looked...

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:44.540
a little like the curling figure under my finger...

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.150
There's nothing to do.

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:20.490
There's never anything to do.

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:23.450
This is different. Very different!

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:28.440
Don't you remember how we shined
during the cultural festival?

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:33.140
I'm bored now that we're 
back to our ordinary lives.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:34.030
Yeah.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:36.940
And there's nothing to 
do during class, either.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:41.120
Shouldn't you be paying attention 
to the lesson during class?

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.140
Anyway, let's have lunch.

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:46.150
I'm so hungry.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.150
Seriously?

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:47.520
Huh? What?

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.270
<b>Wet Paint. Do Not Enter.</b>

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.730
<b>Cafeteria-Store</b>

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:04.320
I'm finally getting to eat in the cafeteria!

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.040
It's been a while since we last came here.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.170
There are some free seats over there.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.360
Well, we did come all the way down here, after all.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:18.010
So cheap!

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:20.010
Udon for 250 yen!

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:23.600
They've got more on the 
menu than I expected.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:25.040
All right!

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:27.470
I'm gonna eat everything on their menu!

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:30.020
That might be difficult.

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:32.450
They have daily specials.

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:34.470
It's different every day.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:38.110
What? Then, I'll have to come 
here every day!

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:41.660
That's right. This day 
will never come again.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:45.840
Eating everything on the menu's 
easier said than done!

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:46.650
Get out of the way.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:49.050
What are you doing, Kanamecchi?

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:50.910
It's your fault for taking so long to order.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:52.590
Like I'm letting you ahead!

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:56.300
The first one to order shall be me, Chi-

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:57.720
Achoo.

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:01.040
Hey! What was that for, Yukki?

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.470
Sorry, I've got a cold.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:05.840
Cough, cough.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:06.780
Next.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.240
Kitsune udon with extra noodles.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:11.020
You're healthy!

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:13.130
Damn it.

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:14.850
That cheat.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:17.490
Shun-chan.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.040
Over here.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.000
What is it?

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.910
Cinderella's working in the cafeteria!

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:35.030
You're right. She's beautiful.

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:36.280
I know, right?

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:37.420
Yukki!

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.320
Yukki, look! Over here!

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.420
Yeah, I saw.

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:44.480
What's wrong with you? You're no fun.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:49.050
Yuki-kun's not all that interested 
in his surroundings.

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:52.370
Excuse me...

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:54.060
Yes?

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:57.800
I thought I ordered kitsune udon...

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:58.310
What?

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:02.780
I completely forgot. I'm so sorry.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:05.700
You're welcome to have the tempura too if you'd like.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:07.530
But...

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:12.490
Take it. Just think of it 
as a token of my love for you.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:16.010
If only I were twenty years younger...

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:18.670
<i>You're making it harder to take it.</i>

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:23.760
Everyone, there's a cougar killer over here!

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:31.960
With its warm food and beautiful Cinderella,

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:34.450
the cafeteria's a pretty great place.

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:36.540
It's getting cold up on the roof.

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:38.480
Why don't we eat inside for a while?

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:39.520
Good idea.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.180
I agree.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:42.380
What?

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:45.120
Someone's not happy with your idea.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:49.600
I won't be able to collect stickers 
if we eat here every day.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:50.580
Stickers?

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:52.490
Yeah, from the convenience store.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:57.610
If I collect thirty points 
from buying bread, I get a plate.

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:00.810
You only have nine points.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:01.970
That's what I mean...

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:05.380
I'll never get enough if 
we eat here every day.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:08.360
Why don't you bring your 
convenience store bread here?

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:11.860
Watching all of you eat cafeteria food...

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:13.640
would make me want some, too.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:16.890
<i>This kid can be quite the handful sometimes...</i>

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:19.940
Okay, I'll help you!

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:23.300
Let's all help Yukki collect stickers!

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:26.170
You shouldn't promise something 
if you don't mean it.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:29.660
I want to shine! Live the festival again!

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:32.030
Sure, but how?

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:38.470
Why don't we rotate who eats the bread...

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:40.690
and give all the stickers to Yukki?

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:43.550
We'll call it "Sticker Duty!"

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:45.920
How groundbreaking.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:47.920
I'll help.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:52.310
It's decided! Let's start tomorrow.

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:53.700
Who'll go first?

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:55.510
Me, me, me! I'll do it!

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:57.180
Why won't you give me any extra?

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:59.670
We don't hand out freebies.

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:00.970
That's a lie.

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:05.850
I saw you give someone 
tempura and fried tofu.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:10.370
Is he talking about Yuki's 
mix up with his udon?

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:12.620
Cinderella's in trouble!

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:15.180
Go help her out.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:15.960
Why?

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:18.700
Don't say that. Hurry up!

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:24.210
Cinderella's a delicate girl who 
can't stand up for herself!

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:29.930
She's waiting for her prince 
to ride up on his white horse!

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:31.430
You're going?!

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:36.420
Come on. We're growing boys.

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:39.430
If you give us something extra, 
we'll take you to the movies.

00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:40.020
Enough.

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:42.920
What?

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.090
You think I'd want to go out with two little boys...

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:47.110
who make a fuss over a little bit of food?

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:49.060
You should learn to support yourselves...

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:52.320
before you even think about asking out a girl again.

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:59.700
Cinderella was amazing at lunch.

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:02.850
She shut them up good.

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:04.410
You just grabbed a towel and came back...

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:06.970
since there was nothing for you to do, Chizuru.

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:07.420
Pu.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:08.830
Shut up!

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:13.690
It just means I'll only be a 
prince for my one true love!

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:14.600
Your one true love?

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:16.710
Um, never mind.

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:17.680
<b>Cafeteria-Store</b>

00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:17.680
Never mind.

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:20.930
Excuse me.

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:27.510
Yes, thanks for waiting.

00:08:27.510 --> 00:08:28.070
Oh.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:31.000
Thanks for lunch.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:32.580
You run the store?

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:38.030
Yes. Sorry, but we're about to eat lunch.

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:41.020
Did you need something?

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:48.200
Yukki, she's asking you what you want.

00:08:50.770 --> 00:08:51.510
Oh, that.

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:55.130
Can I have that, please?

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:56.750
That?

00:08:56.750 --> 00:08:58.100
That, please.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:05.060
Unbelievable!

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:09.270
My daughter's <i>not</i>-for-sale!

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:12.580
What's gotten into you?

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:14.380
There's an order to these things!

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:16.450
You start with something like sharing a diary!

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:17.450
That's not what I meant.

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:19.160
Kayo, Kayo! Come here!

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.620
What is it, Mother?

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:25.120
This kid's got business with you!

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:27.970
What?

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:32.760
Um, I was wondering if I could have that...

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:35.640
It's half-eaten.

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:37.380
I mean the bag.

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:40.810
The bag? Sure.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.560
Actually, I wanted the sticker.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.770
The sticker? I can't give you that.

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:52.520
Just give him the sticker, Kayo.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:56.780
I'm collecting them. He can't have it.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:58.880
Can't you make an exception?

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:00.200
Come on!

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.610
He's really desperate!

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:03.870
How do you figure that?

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:07.540
Collect them yourself instead 
of taking them from others.

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:13.140
I'm in the harsh situation of needing
 to collect 30 points worth.

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:15.120
So does everyone else!

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:17.330
Who cares about one little plate?

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:22.790
You have that thing, don't you,
 the Yamawaki plate I got for you.

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:26.310
Don't say that in front of 
them! You're embarrassing me!

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:28.560
I'm the one who's embarrassed!

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:33.350
The daughter I've raised won't 
even give someone a measly sticker!

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:35.240
That has nothing to do with stickers!

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:37.290
Why are you so stubborn?

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:38.910
Do you know how hard I've worked 
to collect these stickers?

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.910
I'm so embarrassed, my face is on fire.

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:40.950
I'll never give it away.

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:00.010
Oh, sorry.

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:04.930
You really are collecting stickers.

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:07.240
It's the girl from the store.

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:08.980
You came to buy bread, didn't you?

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:11.210
I don't need to buy bread every day...

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:13.730
because we're starting 
Sticker Duty...

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:18.060
but I'll get points faster if I buy bread as well,

00:11:18.060 --> 00:11:19.660
so I'm not sure what to do.

00:11:20.220 --> 00:11:22.410
What's Sticker Duty?

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:25.460
Are you sleepy?

00:11:25.930 --> 00:11:27.970
No, I'm fine.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:29.260
I see.

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:34.130
It's unusual for a high 
school boy to want a plate.

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:36.090
You're into this sort of thing?

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:37.090
I guess.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:38.510
Hm...

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:43.010
I'm collecting stickers 
because I like them, too.

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:47.390
Do you read anime magazines?

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:49.270
What magazines?

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:52.410
<i>Guess not.</i>

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:53.400
What magazines?

00:11:53.780 --> 00:11:54.660
Nothing.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:12:00.320
Hey, how many points do you have?

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:04.510
What's so funny?

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:10.080
Sorry. It's just cute that you've got
 only got one point stickers on your sheet.

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:16.020
So many two's and three's... and a four.

00:12:16.020 --> 00:12:19.340
A student can't afford a bread worth four points.

00:12:19.790 --> 00:12:24.550
Just goes to show what a working 
adult with a salary can do.

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:29.210
Did the four point sticker come from 
the extra large yakisoba bread?

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:33.270
Wh-What's your point? I'd wanted to try it for a while.

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:35.000
Did you finish it all?

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:36.440
Why do you care?

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:37.770
Are you sure?

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:39.440
I've gotta go.

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:40.310
It's fine. No one will know.

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:43.750
<i>I guess I don't have to get one today.</i>

00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:44.700
Huh?

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:47.240
This one doesn't have a sticker.

00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:50.830
Wait!

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:54.680
You girls...

00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:59.310
You took the sticker off this bread, didn't you?

00:12:59.310 --> 00:12:59.880
What?

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:01.710
The sticker.

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:05.690
You can't take the stickers 
without buying the bread!

00:13:06.070 --> 00:13:07.470
Hand it over.

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:11.810
Kids these days...

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:14.680
Huh? Where'd he go?

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:18.390
Why'd you run away?

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:23.320
No one screams about stickers in a store.

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:25.400
I'm pretending I don't know you.

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:26.450
You're doing what?

00:13:26.450 --> 00:13:29.010
I didn't yell because I wanted to.

00:13:30.560 --> 00:13:32.760
Are you saying you don't care...

00:13:32.760 --> 00:13:36.020
if people take stickers without buying the bread?

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:38.280
I do care.

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:39.000
See?

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:42.250
What a ridiculous morning.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:46.360
What?

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:47.620
Nothing.

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:50.740
You should get to school.

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:52.010
You'll be late.

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:53.400
Right...

00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:57.600
Huh? Yukki.

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:00.570
You're up early.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:05.640
I'm on Sticker Duty today, so I 
thought I'd buy it before school.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:10.300
I recommend the extra large yakisoba bread.

00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:12.270
The what?

00:14:18.110 --> 00:14:21.650
Can't you enjoy your food more?

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:23.890
You're making mine taste worse.

00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:27.080
But it's so hard.

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:29.950
Chizuru, don't you usually put away 
two slices of bread easily?

00:14:29.950 --> 00:14:33.680
It's mentally challenging.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:35.310
You're all eating cafeteria food,

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:37.810
and I have to eat convenience store bread.

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:39.980
I feel left out.

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:41.500
What are you saying?

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:44.500
You're the one who came up with Sticker Duty.

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:45.870
It's your own fault.

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:48.360
No, it's your fault.

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:54.510
It's fine, just wave your delicious
 food in my face while you're eating it.

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:58.330
This bread's so good.

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:01.130
Chizuru-kun, take this.

00:15:01.970 --> 00:15:06.130
Thanks. You're the only one who's 
always nice to me, Shun-chan.

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:08.250
Don't baby him, Shun.

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:12.860
He'll always be stupid 
if you don't stop that.

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:14.410
What did you say?

00:15:14.410 --> 00:15:18.930
Since you're always mean to me, take this!

00:15:20.610 --> 00:15:22.630
What do you think you're eating?

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:26.910
You won't miss one. Besides, 
it's not even that good.

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:29.710
Then, spit it out. Come on.

00:15:29.710 --> 00:15:34.220
Stop it, you'll make me dribble the juice!

00:15:34.220 --> 00:15:36.240
Sounds like it's delicious!

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:37.640
Not true!

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:38.640
Quiet down.

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:38.970
You bonehead! Spit it out!

00:15:38.970 --> 00:15:42.130
You will spit it out!

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:43.750
What's wrong with them enjoying their meal?

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:47.370
You're too nice to them.

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:50.300
Who cares? They're just having fun.

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:54.180
They're obviously that loud because they're fighting.

00:15:58.930 --> 00:15:59.920
Shun-chan.

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:02.060
Masaki-chan.

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:06.070
I'm surprised you knew we'd be here.

00:16:06.070 --> 00:16:10.020
I figured you'd be here 
since they closed the roof off.

00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:14.570
S-Sorry. Looks like you're not done eating.

00:16:14.930 --> 00:16:16.260
That's okay.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:17.790
Do you need help with your homework?

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:25.720
What are you having trouble with?

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:26.790
This one.

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:30.280
I had trouble with this one, too.

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:31.590
You did?

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.900
Yes. You should start by solving this bit here.

00:16:33.900 --> 00:16:35.800
Oh, I see.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:39.760
What's wrong with you?! Stop it!

00:16:45.180 --> 00:16:46.500
I don't care.

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:49.400
I'll just eat the food Shun-chan gave me.

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:56.070
Huh? It won't come out.

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:57.910
What's wrong with this thing?

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.330
Damn it. There!

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:08.460
<b>Boys' Bathroom</b>

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:09.610
Sorry, Shun-chan.

00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:10.960
It's okay.

00:17:12.220 --> 00:17:14.570
Class is starting.

00:17:14.570 --> 00:17:18.190
If it isn't washed off now, it'll stain!

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:20.810
Thank you.

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:24.140
I'm the one who sprayed you.

00:17:32.100 --> 00:17:33.890
Hey...

00:17:33.890 --> 00:17:34.710
Yes?

00:17:35.190 --> 00:17:37.550
Shun-chan, do you not have one?

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:39.100
Not have what?

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:40.860
Well... as in...

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:44.240
someone you like?

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:46.610
I mean...

00:17:46.610 --> 00:17:52.270
I thought it'd be nice to talk about 
stuff we don't usually discuss!

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:57.130
Someone I like?

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:00.680
Not at the moment, I guess.

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:04.680
I see.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:06.730
I see.

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:09.610
Chizuru-kun, what about you?

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:11.690
What? M-Me?

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:14.950
I'm, you know...

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:17.800
Sh-Shun-chan!

00:18:18.270 --> 00:18:20.070
I'm falling, Chizuru-kun.

00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:24.650
I hope your uniform doesn't stain.

00:18:25.510 --> 00:18:27.150
It's fine.

00:18:28.320 --> 00:18:31.460
I wonder about everyone else, though.

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:32.340
Wonder about what?

00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:35.670
If there's anyone they like.

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:46.080
<b>Wet Paint. Do Not Enter.</b>

00:19:02.850 --> 00:19:04.120
You!

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:08.540
Good timing! Could you 
wipe some tables down for me?

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:11.060
I came to buy a notebook.

00:19:11.060 --> 00:19:12.880
I cut my finger.

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:14.820
See?

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:18.790
I can't leave until I finish 
this, so I want your help.

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:21.290
I'll come back tomorrow.

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:24.950
Hey.

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:29.140
Want some stickers?

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:32.650
How many points will you give me?

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:38.530
Don't wipe them like that!

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:42.030
Don't brush the litter from the table onto the floor!

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:44.580
We'll have to sweep the floor again!

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:48.380
<i>This better be worth at least three points.</i>

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:51.530
There you go again! How many times is that?

00:19:54.660 --> 00:19:57.250
Hey, what are you going 
to do with the plate?

00:19:57.680 --> 00:19:59.790
Are you going to eat curry rice on it?

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:04.390
I don't think I'd eat curry on it.

00:20:04.860 --> 00:20:05.430
Huh?

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:08.220
The plate would probably turn yellow.

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:13.260
I probably won't use it for 
anything else, either.

00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:15.400
What? You were listening?

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:18.090
I'm listening.

00:20:18.890 --> 00:20:20.440
You're right.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:22.860
Even if you get the plate, you can't use it.

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:24.450
The art's too cute!

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:30.420
But my mom doesn't get it, 
so she always tries to use it.

00:20:30.810 --> 00:20:31.860
I see.

00:20:31.860 --> 00:20:33.750
It's getting dark.

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:36.920
Pick up the pace. I need to go soon.

00:20:37.670 --> 00:20:39.300
Are you going somewhere?

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:42.270
No, we just eat dinner early.

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:44.750
My mom goes to bed early.

00:20:45.250 --> 00:20:48.810
You go straight home to eat dinner?

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:52.540
It's just my mom, and I'm an only child.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:56.040
I don't want to make my mom eat alone.

00:20:57.010 --> 00:21:02.280
She just watches TV when 
I'm not there, though.

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:05.950
Are you finished? Good work.

00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:20.220
Thanks for the help.

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:22.050
What about my sticker?

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:24.590
Oh, I forgot.

00:21:27.040 --> 00:21:27.970
<i>Again...</i>

00:21:36.510 --> 00:21:39.400
It won't come off. Sorry.

00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:41.960
Try a little harder.

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:55.330
So you got one point.

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:56.450
That's great.

00:21:56.760 --> 00:22:00.260
That was definitely three 
points' worth of work.

00:22:00.730 --> 00:22:02.540
Is this the sticker she gave you?

00:22:03.370 --> 00:22:05.300
Yeah, that's it.

00:22:05.720 --> 00:22:10.580
She must be nice to give you a 
sticker when she's collecting them too.

00:22:10.580 --> 00:22:11.510
She's pretty, too.

00:22:11.900 --> 00:22:12.950
Pretty...

00:22:15.710 --> 00:22:18.660
No, she's not pretty.

00:22:18.660 --> 00:22:19.590
Really?

00:22:19.590 --> 00:22:20.380
Yeah.

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:27.020
It looked a little like the 
curling figure under my finger.

00:22:27.960 --> 00:22:32.040
The next time I saw that 
hair was behind my eyelids.

00:22:32.730 --> 00:22:34.940
What should I eat at the cafeteria today?

00:22:35.370 --> 00:22:38.220
Yuki, aren't you on Sticker Duty today?

00:22:38.220 --> 00:22:39.920
What? No way.

00:22:39.920 --> 00:22:44.960
Crescent Moon Silhouette

00:24:16.350 --> 00:24:18.900
Next time: Middle School Diary

00:24:16.350 --> 00:24:19.790
Middle School Diary
